MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_001: Hyaah!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_002: Hah!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_003: Ngaah!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_004: Hup!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_005: No way! How'd you dodge that?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_006: There! An opening!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_007: Agh... You don't mess around, do you, Ultand?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_008: Sorry about that. I might've gotten carried away.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_009: But you're not the easiest opponent, so I had to\nfight hard.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_010: Your attacks were making my hands numb.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_011: Well, you blocked everything I threw at you. Would\nhave been nice if I'd gotten at least one hit.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_012: Especially since your spear isn't all that sharp.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_013: Even though you keep your speed down, I still\ncouldn't get any attacks through.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_014: And here I was, confident in the spear skills that Pop\ntaught me.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_015: Better train some more! Hehehe.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_016: It does feel good to get such high praise from the\nspear protégé of Windstorm Castor.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_017: Eh... Where'd you learn spear fighting, Ultand?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_018: Centurio. With very strict lessons.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_019: Aah! I forgot that Centurio put me on starlogging\nduty tonight!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_020: Starlogging?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_021: Looking at the stars and noting their appearances.\nIt's kind of like a diary that we all keep.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_022: It's said that, in a distant land, a curtain of light\nbearing Aurora's name descends upon the sky.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_023: Some say it's red, some say it's green. No one in\nDagda has ever seen it.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_024: But since it's probably going to show up someday,\nwe've been taking turns to keep a lookout for it.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_025: Oh! Well, shouldn't you get going then?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_026: Yes! See you later!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_027: Ultand! Look out for that water trough!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_028: Eeyah! Oh, I'm so sorry!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_029: Heheh. Ultand's kind, but she can be careless.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_030: I bet if I had a sister, she'd be just like that.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_031: It's strange though...
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_C_032: Why couldn't I land a hit on her?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_001: Oof...
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_002: Come on—keep it up!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_003: Hrgh... I've got a few tricks to— Ngaah!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_004: Noah! Are you alright?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_005: Ohhh...
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_006: Oh my goodness. Are you OK?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_007: Hey! Ultand! Give a guy some personal space!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_008: Good. Looks like you're recovering. I'm so sorry.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_009: You lost your footing in that puddle, and then you\ntook a direct blow.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_010: I'm fine. Never mind that. What was that name\nI heard?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_011: That would be Noah. It's the name of my brother\nwho's about six years younger than me.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_012: I got a little flustered, and I just kind of blurted it out.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_013: Oh! So do I look a little bit like Noah, then?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_014: You do. But it's not just that. Sometimes I mistake\nAurora for my younger sister.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_015: My mom? But she's so much older than you.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_016: It's her vibe, her aura. The two of you look a\nbit similar.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_017: Come to think of it, the two of you hold your spears\nexactly the same way.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_018: Spears? Do you spar with my mom?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_019: Almost every day. Aurora is passionate about\nher training.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_020: She learned how to fight with a spear the same way\nyou did, from Castor.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_021: He'd come up in conversation sometimes, and she'd\ntell me her lovey-dovey stories. It was awkward.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_022: Hahaha. It'd be awkward for me, too, to hear stories \nlike that.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_023: Hey, maybe there's a reason you can read me so well.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_024: Right. You and Aurora had the same teacher, so your\nstyles are practically identical.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_025: That's not fair! Ultand, you're cheating!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_026: I'm not cheating you—I'm training you. Listen,\nCenturio's much stronger than me, right?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_027: So if I can't beat you, I'll never have a chance of\nbeating someone really strong, like Centurio?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_028: If that's the case, let's keep going! Give me all\nyou've got!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_B_029: Hahaha! You look just like Noah when you get\nriled up.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_001: Cai, may I speak with you for a moment?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_002: You're acting all formal, Ultand. What's going on?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_003: I want to apologize for getting myself trapped in that\nZenzele painting. I let my guard down.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_004: I exposed you to such a dangerous situation, and I'm\nvery sorry about that.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_005: Don't be ridiculous! You didn't do anything wrong.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_006: Didn't you tell me I was like a little brother to you?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_007: We're not strangers. We're family.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_008: Helping you was like helping a sister.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_009: Cai...
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_010: Look, I didn't grow up with a big family.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_011: Me and Pop. That was it.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_012: But listening to all your stories makes me think a\nbigger family could be fun.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_013: That's why I have to save Pop, so he and my mom\nand me can be a family.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_014: That's my goal. That's why I'm fighting.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_015: And here you are helping me. So no apologies, got it?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_016: Hehehe. Well, well. Little brother stepping up with a\nlecture for big sis.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_017: Cai, thank you. Truly.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_018: Of course! I'm just glad we got you back safe\nand sound.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_019: You're a really important person to me, Ultand.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_020: Can't have you snatched up by a creep like Zenzele.\nNo way.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_021: When you say "important," what exactly do\nyou mean?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_022: You mean "important" like a sister is\n"important," right?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_023: Uh... Well... I guess... I'm not even sure what I mean.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_024: Mm-hmm... Not sure what you mean...
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_025: Well, how about I keep on as your big sister for now?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_026: I could see us being a real family someday, though.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_027: Then let's be a real family!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_028: Huh? Really?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_029: Yeah! I mean, my mom and dad would welcome you!
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_030: That's very sweet, but it's not exactly what I had\nin mind.
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_031: Oh yeah?
MID_SE_Kai_Hur_A_032: Let's just say we might want to pick up this\nconversation again when you're older.